{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/630776-werewolf-and-______-not-killing-each-other","id":630776,"title":"Werewolf and ______ not killing each other","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-18T00:10:30-07:00","id":630776,"title":"Werewolf and ______ not killing each other","content":"Generally speaking the books say that if you are not either a spirit/fae/shaman/ and in some cases new age style/Druidic witch you will be attacked on sight the moment a werewolf relises what you are, and in some cases even these groups of people get attacked on sight. So is there a way for a vampire/ hermetic/ fallen ect. To not be emediatly hated by the werewolf whom they encounter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3965-andresmo23","name":"Andresmo23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T03:24:20-07:00","id":630910,"title":"","content":"You do realise the Werewolves are terrorist zealots who serve their God unto the Apocalypse? It's not very likely to happen, but most critters have human interests and concerns. It's possible that they might find a common interest before they figure out they are monsters, but what happens after that is most likely not going to end well, even if they love each other to bits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T07:21:49-07:00","id":631154,"title":"","content":"Note that if you try to visit Garou at a caern, they'll kill you as a matter of course. They'd be executed if they didn't under the last tenet of the litany, anyway. When it comes to the tenets about the Veil and protecting caerns, they do not fuck around. Even Black Spiral Dancers defend hives in this manner, and they don't do it alongside vampires, mages, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T07:43:49-07:00","id":631172,"title":"","content":"Are you trying to justify NPC Garou not killing other beings, or convincing PC Garou not to kill NPC's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T08:08:43-07:00","id":631189,"title":"","content":"You'd probably have better luck convincing a member of the Westboro Baptist Church to officiate a same sex wedding than convince a Garou to not rip into tiny pieces a Vampire/Mage/Demon and if a Caern is involved you'd have a better chance of convincing the Pope to perform a same sex wedding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T08:13:40-07:00","id":631193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/630776-werewolf-and-______-not-killing-each-other?p=631172#post631172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you trying to justify NPC Garou not killing other beings, or convincing PC Garou not to kill NPC's.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fairly important question. There are ways to do both, I think, and make it work in a story.<br /> <br /> You've got a fair bit of freedom, I think, if you're trying to justify NPC actions. Garou are fanatics, sure, but they're still people, and people will occasionally make compromises out of self interest or the greater good. So, if there's a mage who might have some useful knowledge about local Fomori activities, it might be worth letting the guy live (for now), assuming he doesn't do one of the deal-breaking transgressions like invade a Caern. Another option might be to have one of the Totems specifically ask/order that the mage be kept alive for now. You'd have to have a good justification for this in the story, of course.<br /> <br /> PCs are harder, because you can't really be sure what they'll do. I don't run Werewolf, but when I've had kill happy players in other games, I've found some ways to deal with it. For example, if a PC Garou kills an NPC mage, perhaps he triggers some lingering magickal effect, or had disrupted a ritual, which leads to something troublesome. I've always liked the idea of some kind of inconvenient transformation curse, because then the Garou has a lot of reason to play nice with other NPCs in an attempt to fix it. Once (IF) it does get fixed, the PC/group will probably be a lot less likely to kill on sight. At least without appropriate investigation. Another time, I've gone the &quot;so you killed him, and he had this MYSTERIOUS PLOT HOOK OBJECT in his pocket&quot; route. All sorts of trouble can come about from the dead guy being unable to answer questions, and you've set up a new adventure for your players. After a while, they'll get more used to actually talking to NPCs before making with the killing of them.<br /> <br /> With regard to specific supernatural types, I think Vampires are probably screwed regardless. There's too much Wyrm taint there for anything but the most desperate kind of alliance, and even then, I'd be surprised if the Vampire made it out alive. Possibly that wouldn't apply to vampires who've got very high humanity or achieved Golconda?<br /> <br /> Demons are an interesting case, because it would depend on which aspect you're linking to Wyrm Taint. If it's just general exposure to the Abyss, or having Fallen, then they're probably screwed like the Vampire. If Wyrm Taint specifically correlates to Torment, then perhaps a low Torment demon could convince the Garou not to kill her.<br /> <br /> Mages/Changelings/Mummies probably have the best chance of getting out of a Garou encounter without a bloodbath (I'd be very cautious if I were a Euthanatos with jhor though), but they should still be cautious. Garou are temperamental.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T08:13:50-07:00","id":631194,"title":"","content":"What about the Shadow Lords, IIRC they are often known for using deception in regards to fighting vampires. Wouldn't they be more likely to work with a vampire, if only to ruin their schemes and get close to kill them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T08:19:13-07:00","id":631208,"title":"","content":"Probably? There are always exceptions to any generality. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T09:51:37-07:00","id":631271,"title":"","content":"What is the situation? The Veil/Masquarade/etc can be enough to keep a certain civility. There something even worse coming? Set was able to get a lot of various critters to put their crap aside and focus on him. And who's the player and who's the NPC? Is there anything you can fudge a little? (Use a Mummy or Anasasi instead of a Vampire, use a Werecat instead of a Werewolf.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T14:29:34-07:00","id":631559,"title":"","content":"I also thought the worse part of Werewolf is how hard it is to make work any plot that involve them NOT killing anything that isn't a werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T16:00:13-07:00","id":631693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/630776-werewolf-and-______-not-killing-each-other?p=631559#post631559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also thought the worse part of Werewolf is how hard it is to make work any plot that involve them NOT killing anything that isn't a werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. The entire &quot;kill anybody on sight who isn't us&quot; aspect of Werewolf really limited things unless a Storyteller was willing to bend that trend a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T17:32:19-07:00","id":631761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/630776-werewolf-and-______-not-killing-each-other?p=631693#post631693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Absolutely. The entire &quot;kill anybody on sight who isn't us&quot; aspect of Werewolf really limited things unless a Storyteller was willing to bend that trend a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's rather overblown, considering that the Garou are often described as not having the resources necessary to persecute wars against vampires and mages, and don't generally have the inclination to hunt down and slay changelings even if they are present in force; wraiths generally don't even have much contact with them, and the knowledge that ghosts are different from ancestor-spirits generally results in moments of existential dread and thanks to Gaia that they don't have to deal with that rather than a crusade. It's more about the attitude than the end result - while they might not kill vampires on sight, a majority of Garou really, really want to rip the vampires' heads off. It's still a tiny, cold candle of hate compared to the burning orb in the sky that is the hate-on that the Mokole have for vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T18:35:29-07:00","id":631809,"title":"","content":"Garou kill other supernaturals like they don't violate the tenets of the Litany.<br /> <br /> And since Metis are playable because they're not so rare...<br /> <br /> Yeah. Ideals/what the Garou say, does not match up at all with what the Garou do.<br /> <br /> The books are actually chock full of examples of Garou not attacking things on sight; as long as they don't feel a Caern is in danger (which is basically self-defense at that point).<br /> <br /> Of course, there's always the fact that plenty of supernaturals are powerful enough that the Garou can't just steamroll them to consider. Garou have very few ways of indirectly determining how powerful another supernatural critter is. Not liking mages is all fine and dandy, but most Garou aren't stupid enough to attack one without a good reason. They have no idea if a mage will be lucky to singe them with a minor fireball, or can just teleport a whole pack into the middle of the ocean. Risking the second just because mages are icky isn't worth it unless the mage is causing problems.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T19:00:47-07:00","id":631821,"title":"","content":"In all seriousness for a short time Garou can work with others. However and here is the true problem at some point a Garou will frenzy. Garou in frenzy have a difficult time determining friend from foe unless they are packmate. Spirits for the most part will not recognize other creatures of the WOD. This means no pack bond. Garou can and will work with others if the threat is big enough a Technocracy lab targeting kinfolk and The local Hermatic circle team up sure. The Mummy that saved Great Grandma calls to say he needs help killing a local Setite temple sure. The local coffee shop that features live poetry reading and art displays is being attacked by Vampires/Mages/Formori and the local Changelings need help of the Garou sure. The reason is the key there are very few instances where Vampires and Garou will work together in fact one of the few I can think of is the ashtray aka Sam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T20:45:57-07:00","id":631856,"title":"","content":"Sam H. apart, the point isn't that they will make war on everything, or that they never compromise. Surely they do.<br /> <br /> The problem is, that is a rare instance, and sometimes it kills story possibilities.<br /> <br /> One of the best chronicles I played was as a Kindred among Garous. I had Humanity 8 and True Faith in Gaia, being a former Silent Strider Kinfolk and a Salubri, just so I could stand a chance at being accepted by the group. And I was indeed, to the point of residing at the store where they had their Caern. It was fun, it was memorable, but it was only feasible because I made a extremely unlikely snow-flake, used the curiosity of the high-ranking Uktena Theurge to buy time, it was a Glass-Walkers Caern and on top of all that all the relevant Garous at the Caern, including the current elders, where PCs, so they could just do as they saw fit. Oh, and the ST <u>really</u> loved crossovers and snow-flakeism.<br /> <br /> Because, with all that, and all my loyalty, in any &quot;reasonable&quot; game I would be in a very different position. Not that it wouldn't be fun to work a little separated as a convenient outside ally (that was my first goal), but I had to go to insurmountable lengths just for that. Other alleys could be used, but they where all limited.<br /> <br /> Werewolves have a rather narrow worldview, and that is a fact. It isn't impossible to work with it, but sometimes it just isn't worth it. If this happened at your games, gentlemen, what would have happened to my character and her friends?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T21:19:26-07:00","id":631888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/630776-werewolf-and-______-not-killing-each-other?p=631856#post631856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Werewolves have a rather narrow worldview, and that is a fact. It isn't impossible to work with it, but sometimes it just isn't worth it. If this happened at your games, gentlemen, what would have happened to my character and her friends?</div> </div> </div> </div>The same thing that would happen to a mage or garou or a changeling in a Vampire game? Or a vampire (and probably garou or changeling) in a mage game? None of the games are particularly open to crossovers. All of the lines have a Xenophobic theme to them. Garou are just the most openly militant of the lines.<br /> <br /> Any crossover is possible, but for most (if not all) of them, you have to be willing to bend the rules.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T00:34:53-07:00","id":632042,"title":"","content":"Vampire isn't xenophobic, not like that. A werewolf in a vampire chronicle will be seem as a potential threat, potent asset, and something to be aware of. Will have to keep secrets and deal with hidden agendas from everyone.<br /> <br /> But that's how Vampire is supposed to work anyway, for everyone.<br /> <br /> Not that you're completely wrong, and I would actually want a 4th edition where crossover doesn't take such a toll, neither rules nor setting-wise. But even by he current rules there are a HUGE gap between the level of xenophobia from Werewolf and the other lines. Heck, in the main setting (Africa and Asia are almost other planets for cWoD) they are the most xenophobic even among themselves!<br /> <br /> And curiously, with their niche i the setting, this is a shame precisely because they are the most asked for in crossovers as far as I could see. Werewolves are in the best position to deal with another supernatural beings. And are the most dangerous to be around simply because most don't need Rage to actually get mad and end up killing you.<br /> <br /> For the people that tries to explain their level of prejudice on Rage and Frenzy, I would like to remember that vampires, ALSO have those. And believe, though a LOT less xenophobic than your average werewolf, a Brujah vampire isn't less likely to frenzy and tear you to shreds than most lupines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T02:43:31-07:00","id":632107,"title":"","content":"Werewolves in VtM are pretty much presented as:<br /> Bitch is crazy, RUN THE FUCK AWAAAAAY!<br /> <br /> How is that a more positive light?<br /> <br /> The fully justified, socially enforced xenophobia of Werewolf is kinda the point. You cannot really have W:tA without it. It would be Forsaken all over again, and on that I'd prefer to pass (while stealing some totally awesome critters they made along the way).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T03:16:54-07:00","id":632123,"title":"","content":"Do you really think being wary of a creature known for killing on sight is the same level of xenophobia as <b>freaking killing on sight</b>!?<br /> <br /> Given how cWoD is constructed, with the games being separated, but actually not, it is only logical that most creatures avoid werewolves. Specially vampires, given that most of them are caught by Sense the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> The xenophobia of werewolves is far from fully justified, though surely socially enforced. And I do know it is an element of the setting, a very relevant one. But it went too far.<br /> <br /> Seriously, with all the really cool things they made about the Garou and the other Fera, I find Apocalypse extremely boring sometimes, because it have the most rigid limits. And this extreme level of xenophobia is one of my main reasons to get tired of the game for years at a time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T06:29:21-07:00","id":632194,"title":"","content":"Werewolves are people, and people are complex. They are religious zealots who's moral teaching says &quot;combat the wyrm wherever it dwells&quot; pretty basic. Pretty simple. The same group of tenents include &quot;Don't sleep with other garou&quot; and yet there are enough Metis for them to be a playable splat. People are great especially zealots at coming up with reasons for their double think. Maybe the Blank is useful right now, maybe someone fell in love, maybe there's a common enemy or maybe there is just a weird friendship and so and so is &quot;the only good one&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course this is the world of darkness so its not like they don't have a valid point, there haven't been centuries of &quot;Good&quot; vampires, but there have been people holding out the olive branch and getting fucked over for it. There have been Children of Gaia playing peacemaker with Hermetics and having their Caerns taken because they trusted the wrong asshole. Conversely there have been centuries of Shadowlords making alliances and when the Vampire or mage has been at their weakest having them get struck down and the Shadowlords claiming all sorts of Glory for their cunning plan.<br /> <br /> Suffice to say the World of Darkness is complex. Its filled with rational fear not mindless xenophobia. However sometimes people overcome that fear for reasons, and sometimes it works out. But history doesn't remember the 1 time out of 10 it worked out great. It remembers the 9 times it fucked up horribly.<br /> <br /> Or you could run a game that uses the eastern premises, even if you want to use western splats. The Year of the Lotus line presented the idea that while every group still hates each other, still wants to take their shit, politicing and diplomacy is a valid tactic for this as much as murder. V20 introduces the position of consul, its meant to be an ambassador to the enemy sects, that could be adapted to the west having the tense situation of being the Ambassador to the local Sept from the Vampire Court, where they might kill you at any time with the wrong frenzy, where you are hated but they try to be polite try to be civil and try to work things out all the while trying to screw your people over(and vfce versa), after all we had diplomatic relations with the SOviet Union for all of the Cold war and that was all sorts of nasty.<br /> <br /> Really, alot of options as long as you remember characters are people and people are weird.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T10:10:55-07:00","id":632476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/630776-werewolf-and-______-not-killing-each-other?p=631693#post631693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Absolutely. The entire &quot;kill anybody on sight who isn't us&quot; aspect of Werewolf really limited things unless a Storyteller was willing to bend that trend a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire point of the game is to acclimate the players to fighting straight-up slugfests and then unleash the horrible consequences of their actions on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T10:23:52-07:00","id":632499,"title":"","content":"I know.<br /> <br /> As I said, I know there are exceptions. I played as an exception and used as example.<br /> <br /> But at the same time that Metis exist, Metis' parents are screwed over regularly, and Metis themselves usually have the social standing of a sick leprous in the Middle Ages. Again, I ask: what would happen to my character from the previous example, and her friends, if you where the ST?<br /> <br /> Werewolf society is unforgiving. Not only few individuals will go to certain lengths (but sure, some will. There's even a Merit to begin with one vampire friend), but they will have to be extremely paranoid about other Garou just for doing so.<br /> <br /> This is limiting. I'm NOT saying it is impossible to work around it. But it limits severely how you can do it and the logical outcomes.<br /> <br /> Of course, you can also bend the setting. But this is pointless in a discussion about it. In my friend's game, my vampire ended up becoming a respected member of the Nation, if facing hard prejudice sometimes. But this is my friend'd version, not what is supposed to happen by the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T13:13:33-07:00","id":632684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/630776-werewolf-and-______-not-killing-each-other?p=632499#post632499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Of course, you can also bend the setting. But this is pointless in a discussion about it. In my friend's game, my vampire ended up becoming a respected member of the Nation, if facing hard prejudice sometimes. But this is my friend'd version, not what is supposed to happen by the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally don't see it anywhere near as limiting as you say it is. You need to bend any of the settings to allow for any other supernatural to be involved. You are right that a Vampire shouldn't be allowed on a Caern. Vampires wouldn't be allowed to roam around a Chantry either. That doesn't mean a Mage game is too limiting. The various games really aren't that different that way.<br /> <br /> You seem to be saying that because Vampires and Werewolves are enemies, that the game is limiting. The games were never really meant for crossover (any of them), outside of specific book instances. And no one really allows outsiders into the sacred places anyway.<br /> <br /> And to answer directly: in most games I've played in or ran, what your character did would be next to impossible and the Garou running the Caern would have it sieged and probably die. That would be the consequences for allowing a leech to infiltrate their holy site. The Garou being religious zealots isn't a limiting factor in the game in my opinion. It is simply part of the setting. If you are playing Werewolf, in general, you are choosing to play a people at war.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/630776-werewolf-and-______-not-killing-each-other?p=632499#post632499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A werewolf in a vampire chronicle will be seem as a potential threat, potent asset, and something to be aware of. Will have to keep secrets and deal with hidden agendas from everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with your assessment of how this would play out. I think you very much underestimate how supernaturals deal with one another. No other supernaturals would be allowed to wander around Elysium. No Vampire in the right mind would let this happen. A Garou being there wouldn't just be seen a threat or someone to be manipulated. Neither would a Mage. A Changeling might, but that's because players and characters really underestimate them. The Garou would be an extremely short lived character. They would not be treated like any other Vampire. They would most likely be sent on a series of suicide missions until they were dead.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I've played in several crossover games that didn't result is the wholesale death of everyone. The arguments you are making against WtA really just apply to any of the core games.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T16:29:02-07:00","id":632819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/630776-werewolf-and-______-not-killing-each-other?p=632499#post632499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know.<br /> <br /> As I said, I know there are exceptions. I played as an exception and used as example.<br /> <br /> But at the same time that Metis exist, Metis' parents are screwed over regularly, and Metis themselves usually have the social standing of a sick leprous in the Middle Ages. Again, I ask: what would happen to my character from the previous example, and her friends, if you where the ST?</div> </div> </div> </div>A game where both sides try to screw you over. A game where Rivals in the sept use your existence to attack your allies. A game where you run head long into Garou are really bad for your long term humanity, where you'd question your Faith in Gaia and whether the Garou are all wrong. I'd have other packs make deals with the Tremere and with all sorts of hypocritical moralizing explain why their act was Gaian and your very existence is abomination!.<br /> <br /> I'd have high humanity vampires hunting werewolves to defend children who showed up as wyrm tainted just because they were in the wrong place at the wrong time. It would be a very hard game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Werewolf society is unforgiving. Not only few individuals will go to certain lengths (but sure, some will. There's even a Merit to begin with one vampire friend), but they will have to be extremely paranoid about other Garou just for doing so.<br /> <br /> This is limiting. I'm NOT saying it is impossible to work around it. But it limits severely how you can do it and the logical outcomes. </div> </div> </div>Christian society is pretty unforgiving I mean Jesus had alot to say about Violence and being rich and how these are horrible things and as we all know there are no Christians who believe in violence as a first solution to problems and there are no Rich Chiristians right?<br /> <br /> <br /> Or how man homophobes have turned out ot have secret gay lovers?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course, you can also bend the setting. But this is pointless in a discussion about it. In my friend's game, my vampire ended up becoming a respected member of the Nation, if facing hard prejudice sometimes. But this is my friend'd version, not what is supposed to happen by the book. </div> </div> </div>The Kill on Sight is just as much bending the setting as Superfriends.<br /> <br /> Sense wyrm is not Detect Evil. It will show fomori, it will show Vampires it will also show someone exposed to the wrong chemicals or lives in a really shitty apartment. So figuring out what tripped it off is the first step on a chain not &quot;OK CRINOS TIME!&quot;<br /> <br /> Even Truth of Gaiaing out that someone is a vampire the first response shouldn't be CRINOS I mean there's a whole damn auspice dedicated to trickery and intelligence gathering. &quot;WHy is this leech here&quot; should be the first response.<br /> <br /> Werewolves pick their battles. The forces of the wyrm are numberless and the garou are finite. Leeches are generally a passive wyrm problem vs more active stuff like Pentex or BSDs or banes. The general self absorbed nature of Kindred makes them not particularly likely to be actively spreading the wyrm's taint, well no more than assholish humans.<br /> <br /> Of course while the garou nation is riddled with bigotry and all manner of stupidity that has basically shot itself in the foot, that doesn't make them entirely wrong about Kindred. Ignoring the Gaia thing, purely from a VTM perspective most vampires are Low humanity assholes. The next highest group are crazy inhumane monsters. After that you have a small sliver of kindred who can probably be called decent people and most of them are young and going to become jaded assholes given time.<br /> <br /> Humanity's ability to hide wyrm taint is not the approval of Gaia. The Aura of Humanity is concealment, it covers and hides the monster. This is why the Camarilla cling to it even low humanity assholes are better at hiding it than the inhumane monsters. High Humanity not showing up Wyrm tainted is a concealment feature of humanity, nothing more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T21:04:44-07:00","id":633012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/630776-werewolf-and-______-not-killing-each-other?p=631809#post631809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou kill other supernaturals like they don't violate the tenets of the Litany.<br /> <br /> And since Metis are playable because they're not so rare...<br /> <br /> Yeah. Ideals/what the Garou say, does not match up at all with what the Garou do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this.<br /> <br /> People seem to think the setting is much more hardcore than it is - partly a reaction to some ill conceived crossover in the early days, both canonical and by over rambunctious players and STs. Having a foe like the Wyrm - basically Satan - and setting it in the End Days, does much to clarify the mind and set players to kill the bad guys. <br /> <br /> In reality, the Garou live in shades of gray like everyone else. Garou definitely fight the Wyrm, but that is not all they do. And not all Wyrm creatures are equally a threat. In real life, people have to prioritize goals and sacrifice some things in order to get others. Some people are criminals. Some people are apathethic.<br /> <br /> A common problem in fantasy roleplaying is that certain sourcebooks and many gaming groups seem to assume &quot;adventurers&quot; are the common character types and the world is based around people like them. In the real world, &quot;adventurers&quot; (mercenaries, freebooters, hired thugs, adrenalin junkies) are few in number, sometimes despised, and live on the fringes of society. It distorts the setting to assume the world's important characters are similar to PCs or that what they do is normal. But that is what is scaled because that's what the game is about.<br /> <br /> A similar issue affects many portrayals of Werewolf. PCs want to be heroes, so we assume that's what the Garou are overall. In reality, Garou are just as self-serving or heroic as people in real life, which means the PCs actually are probably the most idealistic of the bunch. You'll have some septs that are very traditionalist and very sincere at obeying the Litany. You will have others that almost ignore it completely.<br /> <br /> The Litany is only enforced as much as ordinary Garou take it upon themselves to enforce it. There is no &quot;state&quot; with cops that do it. It's up to personal interpretation and how much one is willing to fight for it in a sept with people who hold different values.<br /> <br /> In the case of other magical creatures, simply killing everyone outright tends to lead to war. I believe the Garou have too many enemies to fight all of them at once. They have to select their battles carefully. A lot of enemies probably escape notice provided they don't threaten major Garou interests like the sanctity of caerns, important kinfolk, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T22:33:49-07:00","id":633117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">vampires wouldn't be allowed to roam around a Chantry either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages would be wary of knew vampires, but most wouldn't be against contact. While in Werewolf you have to keep your vampire ally a secret, in Mage they will probably just say to be cautious. Hollow Ones are <u>known</u> for regular contact with other supernaturals, vampires included. It took one or two years for the Order of Hermes to decide to act against House Tremere once their state was discovered.<br /> <br /> In fact, a lot of Mages could simply get an interest over any supernatural critter, just for research purposes. They can take it and bring to the lab, sure. But they can also want to see the creature &quot;in its habitat&quot; and just take notes. All that without even one step outside the expectations over a Mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">No other supernaturals would be allowed to wander around Elysium.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it depends exclusively on the vampire who runs the particular Elysium, because it isn't nor sacred, nor secret. It is just a neutral ground. Surely most Kindred will be wary of a place that lets a Werewolf inside, but at the same time it would be a tremendous show of power for the one who keeps the Elysium running, or the Prince. Vampires love the eventual show of pure badassery, got the Harpies gossiping to exhaustion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Kill on Sight is just as much bending the setting as Superfriends.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, to a degree. That's why the views of each faction over others are called stereotypes. They're skewed.<br /> <br /> BUT, when Garou and Kindred find each other, the most likely outcome for an unprepared vampire is to be slaughtered. Why? If they found each other at the same time, instead of one splat noticing first the other, it is likely that the Garou will see the vampire as a liability, and kill it so it can't alert other minions of the Wyrm. If the Garou notices first, they will evaluate the vampire as a possible target. It will be mostly seem as an enemy and avoided or confronted as such, so the vampire will either be killed or never notice what happened. So, from a vampire's POV, it IS kill-on-sight most of the times, and it isn't bending anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to be saying that because Vampires and Werewolves are enemies, that the game is limiting. The games were never really meant for crossover (any of them)</div> </div> </div> </div>Given how the settings where constructed, I find this a stupid decision, but I'm aware of that. And yes, that's precisely why I find it limiting in a nut shell, though I would rephrase as &quot;the Werewolves are at war, period&quot;. And don't focus so much on their sacred places, it was an extreme situation and I'm aware of that, also.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is simply part of the setting. If you are playing Werewolf, in general, you are choosing to play a people at war.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah, I know. And to say that the setting isn't limited because it is supposed to work that way is the same as saying that a decorative sword isn't blunt because it is supposed to work that way.<br /> <br /> There are much more to be explored in the setting. But it is a war setting, so...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And to answer directly: in most games I've played in or ran, what your character did would be next to impossible and the Garou running the Caern would have it sieged and probably die. That would be the consequences for allowing a leech to infiltrate their holy site.</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely what I said. And I would love to play such a game, once. But I would need this to happen to begin with, so, limits. And then we would have explored the only way in the game for such a thing to develop, unless the entire sect played an awesome con for the vampire to not be discovered to begin with.<br /> <br /> Limits. Limits everywhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A game where both sides try to screw you over. A game where Rivals in the sept use your existence to attack your allies. A game where you run head long into Garou are really bad for your long term humanity, where you'd question your Faith in Gaia and whether the Garou are all wrong. I'd have other packs make deals with the Tremere and with all sorts of hypocritical moralizing explain why their act was Gaian and your very existence is abomination!.<br /> <br /> I'd have high humanity vampires hunting werewolves to defend children who showed up as wyrm tainted just because they were in the wrong place at the wrong time. It would be a very hard game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shut up, and take my sheet! That seems awesome, really! But, again, once. And I really doubt it would be considered a likely result. Going by the setting, <b>idpersona</b>'s siege seems more likely. Far more likely.<br /> <br /> <br /> Don't need explanation on the setting. I know it. I know how prejudice, violence and bigotry are themes from werewolf. How the setting plays with the theme of the tragic hero(es) that creates his own destiny by trying to avoid it. How it all fits together in one of the most beautiful of all cWoD cosmologies and metaplots.<br /> <br /> Just think that it went too far sometimes, in a way that makes it, yes, even more hostile to crossovers than the other lines. It IS limiting to game, even being an awesome story. By the way, one of the problems with cWoD in general was to make the story more relevant than the playability, and indeed this is just one of the examples. There are others, both in Werewolf and in the other lines, and Vampire isn't at all without its problems. If the limitations in one don't bother you, so be it. But they do exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T22:40:45-07:00","id":633119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/630776-werewolf-and-______-not-killing-each-other?p=633012#post633012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lotsa things</div> </div> </div> </div>Just one relevant detail. Garou society as described in the books is a society at war. It DOES have an effect that sets them apart from common people. And that's actually very realistic to a degree, I never said otherwise. So even most of them being far from heroic, common prejudices and a constant state of war are the main reasons for how Garou society works, turned up to eleven because both the prejudices and the war are out of any mortal proportion in a number of aspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T01:02:05-07:00","id":633262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/630776-werewolf-and-______-not-killing-each-other?p=633117#post633117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages would be wary of knew vampires, but most wouldn't be against contact. While in Werewolf you have to keep your vampire ally a secret, in Mage they will probably just say to be cautious. Hollow Ones are <u>known</u> for regular contact with other supernaturals, vampires included. It took one or two years for the Order of Hermes to decide to act against House Tremere once their state was discovered.<br /> <br /> In fact, a lot of Mages could simply get an interest over any supernatural critter, just for research purposes. They can take it and bring to the lab, sure. But they can also want to see the creature &quot;in its habitat&quot; and just take notes. All that without even one step outside the expectations over a Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hollow Ones are an exception with Kindred.<br /> <br /> Its a Violation of the code of Hermes. The celestial chorus do I really need to explain? The Euthanatos, Verbena and Akashics all seem them as fundimental violations of the natural order, hell a Euthanatos killing a vampire on sight probably is from his perspective an act of mercy. Kindred are spiritually dead and tend to attract banes so not exactly Dreamspeaker friends. This generally leaves only the CoX, Etherites and VA as neutrals and even then vampires are parasites who prey upon humans.<br /> <br /> Of course being killed on Sight is not the worst thing that happens to the would be Kindred found by a mage. the New Progenitors book has all sorts of fun things on what you can do with recycled Reality deviant parts. This is before we get to the fact that Vampires are pinatas full of Magical Heron <br /> <br /> Honestly Kindred probably have MORE reason to fear some random mage finding them out, the Masquerade protects!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're right, to a degree. That's why the views of each faction over others are called stereotypes. They're skewed.<br /> <br /> BUT, when Garou and Kindred find each other, the most likely outcome for an unprepared vampire is to be slaughtered. Why? If they found each other at the same time, instead of one splat noticing first the other, it is likely that the Garou will see the vampire as a liability, and kill it so it can't alert other minions of the Wyrm. If the Garou notices first, they will evaluate the vampire as a possible target. It will be mostly seem as an enemy and avoided or confronted as such, so the vampire will either be killed or never notice what happened. So, from a vampire's POV, it IS kill-on-sight most of the times, and it isn't bending anything. </div> </div> </div><br /> From the perspective of Vampire the Masquerade Lupines are presented as one of many factors trying to keep the characters within the boundries of a single city. Yes going to the woods is treated as a danger but so is going to another city. It could be held by a rival sect. There's a position for &quot;Guy who randomly patrols looking for new people and tries to kill them on sight&quot; its called Scourge and this is in the &quot;Humane&quot; sect.<br /> <br /> The whole of Kindred society is built around trying not to kill eachother on sight and and eat their delicious souls and it generally works. And then we get to the Masquerade/Silence of the blood. Why does this exist? Because humans would kill you on sight. Really its not that Lupines are Unique as a situation that will want to kill kindred. The natural state of kindred condition is to be in a point where some one wants to kill you and you come up with a method that keeps them from doing so(Whether its hiding, being useful, tricking them etc..)<br /> <br /> Conversely from the Apocalypse perspective no Tribebook's opinion on Vampires is as simple as &quot;Kill on Sight&quot;. There are histories of treaties(that the vampires generally break), or giving gruff warnings for vampires to get the fuck out of their territory(which as I said is not all that different from some kindred doing the same).<br /> <br /> Now plenty of people interpret things in black and white but that's not how the books are written. This is before we get into something like &quot;Ok this town has a Beast Court take over the caern because the Garou fucked up. They send an ambassador to the Elysium because that's how they do it in the Old Country!&quot; which is a perfectly easy thing to work out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't need explanation on the setting. I know it. I know how prejudice, violence and bigotry are themes from werewolf. How the setting plays with the theme of the tragic hero(es) that creates his own destiny by trying to avoid it. How it all fits together in one of the most beautiful of all cWoD cosmologies and metaplots.<br /> <br /> Just think that it went too far sometimes, in a way that makes it, yes, even more hostile to crossovers than the other lines. It IS limiting to game, even being an awesome story. By the way, one of the problems with cWoD in general was to make the story more relevant than the playability, and indeed this is just one of the examples. There are others, both in Werewolf and in the other lines, and Vampire isn't at all without its problems. If the limitations in one don't bother you, so be it. But they do exist. </div> </div> </div>The setting isn't written that way, the problem is for some reason online people want to be in one of two camps. &quot;Kill on Sight&quot; or &quot;Superfriends&quot; the books aren't written from either perspective. The problem isn't Werewolf is written wrong its Vampire is written from the perspective of &quot;ok everyone wants to kill you give them a good reason not to&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T05:10:45-07:00","id":633341,"title":"","content":"Except that the Beast Courts would not stoop down to actually conversing with Kindred. The Cainites don't get that luxury as they're not seen as anywhere close to the Kuei Jin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T08:30:07-07:00","id":633500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/630776-werewolf-and-______-not-killing-each-other?p=633341#post633341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that the Beast Courts would not stoop down to actually conversing with Kindred. The Cainites don't get that luxury as they're not seen as anywhere close to the Kuei Jin.</div> </div> </div> </div>That still depends on whether or not they have the reserves to solve the problem. Lone Kindred roving through might evade notice. The Sabbat attempting to replicate the plot of Shiki, though, that requires an immediate response.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T09:12:49-07:00","id":633514,"title":"","content":"I suppose it depends on what Garou were talking about here.<br /> <br /> If a Kindred meets a Get of Fenris, Shadow Lord, Silver Fang, Wendigo, Silent Strider or Red Talon, then yes, that Kindred will most certainly be killed on sight. A Child of Gaia might be more willing to work together if they situation calls for it, but even then as Garou they still perceive Vampires as oddly free-willed Banes or Wyrm-tainted creatures, which means the Litany will demand their destruction.<br /> <br /> There's also the social pressure from other Tribes who will most likely see working with Kindred as a mass betrayal of their society, which could mean that Caern of Children of Gaia are going to be blacklisted from every other local Tribal Caern and could very likely even be attacked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T14:21:30-07:00","id":633786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/630776-werewolf-and-______-not-killing-each-other?p=633341#post633341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that the Beast Courts would not stoop down to actually conversing with Kindred. The Cainites don't get that luxury as they're not seen as anywhere close to the Kuei Jin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Contrary to KJ belief its not their specialness that makes the shen situation work. Its that everyone considers politicing with people they fucking hate a system that works.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Going over things tribe by tribe sort of misses the point. If a Vampire randomly walks onto the Caern he's going to get killed for invading their territory, but that's not all that different from a Scourge or the Hound finding you, death by going into the wrong person's territory is a fact of Kindred life period.<br /> <br /> Now how else are they going to run into the vampire? are we assuming the Werewolf is spamming Truth of Gaia/Scent the wyrm on everyone who passes? Every Hot Goth chick? Every shadey contact they have? Lets assume some basic compitency on the part of the vampire, that they are good at covering for themself, that when the Werewolf finds out its well after they have some sort of relationship at that point and from there the Werewolf has to decide what is worht more.<br /> <br /> Now Frenzy is a hell of a thing, but its also something you have to live with as a kindred, I once saw a fairly tame torey with just a couple dots of celerity, he was mostly auspex and Presence, completely murder an art critc who panned his work in Frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","user":"Lian","date":". 08-20-2015, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T14:48:01-07:00","id":633814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/630776-werewolf-and-______-not-killing-each-other?p=633786#post633786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Contrary to KJ belief its not their specialness that makes the shen situation work. Its that everyone considers politicing with people they fucking hate a system that works.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Going over things tribe by tribe sort of misses the point. If a Vampire randomly walks onto the Caern he's going to get killed for invading their territory, but that's not all that different from a Scourge or the Hound finding you, death by going into the wrong person's territory is a fact of Kindred life period.<br /> <br /> Now how else are they going to run into the vampire? are we assuming the Werewolf is spamming Truth of Gaia/Scent the wyrm on everyone who passes? Every Hot Goth chick? Every shadey contact they have? Lets assume some basic compitency on the part of the vampire, that they are good at covering for themself, that when the Werewolf finds out its well after they have some sort of relationship at that point and from there the Werewolf has to decide what is worht more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quibble over sensory power name: the other in the duo should be Scent of the True Form, not Truth of Gaia. ToG would only apply if you ask someone if they're a vampire and they lie about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now Frenzy is a hell of a thing, but its also something you have to live with as a kindred, I once saw a fairly tame torey with just a couple dots of celerity, he was mostly auspex and Presence, completely murder an art critc who panned his work in Frenzy. </div> </div> </div>There's a joke to be made related to The Critic there, but I can't seem to find it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T16:27:37-07:00","id":633933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/630776-werewolf-and-______-not-killing-each-other?p=633786#post633786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now how else are they going to run into the vampire? are we assuming the Werewolf is spamming Truth of Gaia/Scent the wyrm on everyone who passes? Every Hot Goth chick?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, only player characters act that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T18:50:59-07:00","id":634148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/630776-werewolf-and-______-not-killing-each-other?p=633933#post633933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, only player characters act that way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Players who's characters have time to spam gifts looking for vampires clearly need stuff to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T22:54:55-07:00","id":634259,"title":"","content":"Well first off, werewolves DON'T just run around killing whatever the shizzle lands in their crosshairs. First thing, they're mostly unaware of when that happens. Seriously, the Masquerade works. Smart mages are subtle. no one believes in fairies, and ghosts are off being freaking <i>dead</i>. The Garou could be standing in line at subway with a Sluagh, a Choirster, and a Ventrue (...why? Maybe he needs the blood of people who handle black forest ham regularly) and none of the four would be any wiser about it. <br /> <br /> But say one of them somehow &quot;slips.&quot; The Sluagh is suddenly attacked by a chimera, or the Mage has crazy resonance, or the Ventrue is wearing sunglasses at night or whatever. What's the garou going to do? Most often, get out of the way of the weirdo. Why? because nine times out of ten, <i>it's not worth the Garou's time</i>. first off, jumping in s a risk to the Veil. Second, it's hard enough fighting the war against the Wyrm without getting dragged into the wacky bullcrap of the other freaks of the night. And really, you're in line at a subway, <i>it's not important</i>. Now, if one of these weirdoes starts doing something the garou sees as a threat, that's one thing. But just &quot;oh, that jackass is a vampire!&quot; probably isn't going to get much of a response beyond &quot;I saw a stupid vampire at subway tonight.&quot;<br /> <br /> It takes time and effort to kill these things, after all. And some of them are tougher than you would think. And then there's ramifications. I don't care how tough Garou are, starting a turf war with the local brujah or redcaps is not going to be a walk in the park. Mages are even worse. and what do you get out of it? A point of Glory, maybe? You get to be known as the guy who thinks a biker ate his arm, too.<br /> <br /> So then. it's just not worth the Garou's while to go full-on pogrom against the various supernatural weirdoes they might accidentally bump into. Those resources have to be pointed at bigger, badder threats these days.<br /> <br /> There's your &quot;in.&quot; Whatever critter you're throwing at them <i>will</i> have time to say its peice - unless it jumps in while they're at war, or decides to visit a caern or something dumb like that. The tricky part is getting the Garou to <i>care</i>. Seriously you're fighting a cosmological, generational war for the literal soul of hte universe against what is tangibly, objectively the manifestation of Evil\u2122, and this finger-waggler thinks you have time for him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T00:33:41-07:00","id":634335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/630776-werewolf-and-______-not-killing-each-other?p=633786#post633786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now how else are they going to run into the vampire? are we assuming the Werewolf is spamming Truth of Gaia/Scent the wyrm on everyone who passes?</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems to rather significantly underestimate what the Garou can do; especially the city Tribes (who are the most likely to run into vampires). Bone Gnawers have a Rank 2 Gift that lets them use Scent of the True Form on a whole city block in one go. So if they think there might be supernatural activity they don't like in an area, they can just plop a Fostern (who also has access to Blissful Ignorance and Guise of the Hound for serious urban stealth) Philodox in the general area and scan everyone around. The Glass Walkers have Cybersenses at Rank 2 as well, which lets them do things like have IR vision at night, letting them see the heat difference between vampires and humans. Both Tribes get Attunement at Rank 4; on top of a suite of Gifts that can ruin any vampire's night at that level without direct conflict.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Every shadey contact they have? </div> </div> </div>Why not? It's overkill for every person on the street, but when you're dealing with questionable folk, and you have access to cheap Gifts to that let you detect Wyrm taint, if someone's a supernatural critter, and so on, why wouldn't you scan them to know what you're dealing with? Werewolves aren't exactly &quot;people persons&quot; so they aren't going to have huge numbers of normal contacts as it is (that's what Kin are for), so anyone they do interact with should probably get this treatment.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T15:09:18-07:00","id":635090,"title":"","content":"The only time I had Garou not kill other beings in a Caern-related situation, was in a certain chronicle.<br /> The players, vampires, had some bad encounters with Fomori and were prone to revenge themselves. One time, one of their contact (a Gangrel) said something about a bunch of &quot;strange looking Nosferatu skulking around the haunted hill in the forest&quot;.<br /> Said hill was in effect a Level 1 Caern recently re-opened by half a couple packs of underdogs. They had 3 Metis guarding the Caern, while the &quot;main&quot; pack was composed by an outcast Shadow Lord (alpha and Philodox), a quasi-ronin Silver Fang (beta and Ahroun), a Bone Gnawers Theurghe and an Uktena Ragabash, and all of them had their own damn relational problems. They were the loser of the Garou world, just a couple steps above Ronins and they had a Caern just because the Shadow Lord Philodox stumbled on it and gathered a pack for the sake of re-opening it (long story...)<br /> <br /> Anyway, the characters encounterd the ShadowLord a lot of times, in various circumstances and they weren't in bad terms (but not too friendly), they knew he roamed around the city, but didn't knew anything of the other werewolves.<br /> So they tripped on a all-out assault on a caern, by a battalion of Fomori and a couple of Black Spirals.<br /> While a couple of characters had problems with Fomori, a couple more wanted to come into the good sides of werewolves and one other was simply too &quot;human&quot; for letting werewolves (the &quot;good ones&quot;) die at the hand of evil-doers.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, they interfered in the assault, saved the Metis that were already taken out, tied and confined the Fomori (memorandum: never send rank-and-file Fomori against a Majesty-wielding Ventrue) and killed the two Spirals, saving in the meanwhile a wolf pup that was in the caern (and that a Spiral was trying to take away).<br /> <br /> In the end, the main pack returned, and find the surprise.<br /> Now, they had moral issues, because two tenets of the Litany were in conflicts:<br /> -Combat the Wyrm Wherever it Dwells and Whenever it Breeds<br /> -Ye Shall Take No Action That Causes a Caern to Be Violated<br /> <br /> But what to do when the &quot;Wyrm&quot; save a Caern from the violation of the Wyrm? (notice the quotes)<br /> the ShadowLord Philodox wanted togive them the benefit of the doubt while the SilverFang Ahroun wanted to kill all of them, regardlessly. The three Metis were dumbfounded and appalled for the fact vampires saved their lifes and Caern, the Gnawers Theurge didn't had the slightest intention of getting in the way and the Ragabash Uktena was simply laughing her socks off.<br /> In the end the Fang challenged the Lord, the two battled, the Lord won and so the character were spared. But it was crystal-clear it was a great moral dilemma for the wolves.<br /> <br /> By the way, the ShadowLord asked them a couple more favors for the sake of &quot;demonstrating their reliability&quot; to the other wolves and then asked some Corax to tail them (but the charactes didn't discoverd it for a lot of time).<br /> But even like this, it was a really borderline situation, were the Garou had really more on their plates than the Kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","user":"Ryoga84","date":". 08-21-2015, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}